            "id": "2095597227515236437",
            "url": "https://x.com/x-user-52/status/2095597227515236437",
            "content": {
              "text": "Astra looking strong on the parts that actually matter: long-horizon SWE and computer use. 75.2% DeepSWE and 72.6% OSWorld Offline is a real jump if it survives messy repos, flaky tests, and UIs that don’t match the sketch.The “AGI Era” line is marketing. The useful test is whether it can take a bug report, reproduce it, patch it, and pass CI without a human cleaning up the last 20%.Rolling out to a few orgs today and “everyone else very soon” is the same cadence as every prior drop. Ship it to Plus/API and let’s see if the demos hold",
